{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/570139-beast-question","id":570139,"title":"Beast: Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-27T04:30:02-07:00","id":570139,"title":"Beast: Question","content":"This has probably already been discussed, and I post on here very rarely, but even though I have helped kickstart Beast to show my support for new venues I still have reservations. In particular how does the myth of the Dark Mother and all monsters being connected &quot;help&quot; the World of Darkness as a whole?<br /> <br /> What I mean is this: when I heard about Beast I was very excited with the concept, you play a human who is not a human who is in fact a monster of ancient myth and the only people who understand you are other monsters in a little bit Addam's Family meets a little bit of Clive Barker's Nightbreed where mostly you just aspire to feed your needs and avoid Heroes. That sound's great. But then this idea crept in that somehow Beasts have the real absolute inside tract on where they come from and this humoring big brother mentality regarding other supernaturals. Except the nWoD is designed with a decentralized mythos in mind, there is no one true ideology, all myths are equally plausible from the perspective of the one spouting it with their own onus of supposed proof. A mage is going to think mage lore is the answer. A vampire is going to think vampiric lore is the answer. And, most importantly to me, a werewolf is going to favor its own lore.<br /> <br /> This is important because when Changing Breeds came out I experienced a lot of people trying to force the Breeds into Forsaken like they were classic Fera when definitively they are not. The Fera are nature's fecundity made manifest. The Forsaken (and Pure) are ancient and storied descendants of a spirit god with a shared language and culture that defies boundaries. They're two different things and, given The People come into conflict with hosts at regular interval, I've always advocated the standard Forsaken response to a human that claims to be a royal ape should be to identify it as a strange kind of host and kill it.<br /> <br /> Now we have Beasts who seem to have an implicit &quot;better than thou&quot; mentality and a mandate to &quot;fill in the blanks&quot; of the world of darkness in such a way that the Beast story supersedes all other subjective beliefs of other supernaturals. That strikes me as a major mistake. But maybe I've just misread the situation. Would someone like to set me straight on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T04:46:04-07:00","id":570154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RuneKnight3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/570139-beast-question#post570139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But then this idea crept in that somehow Beasts have the real absolute inside tract on where they come from and this humoring big brother mentality regarding other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh, every game line does that. Its quite common for the Unchained to classify all supernaturals as failed experiements of the God Machine, or how the Lost think vampires are messed up fetches and werewolves are mutated briar wolves. Mages assume that everything is somehow connected to the Supernal, and originates from, or reflects it, etc.<br /> <br /> The only difference is that Beast is a crossover game, so they're a bit more obvious with the whole thing. But its still nothing more than a local mythology that may or may not be true, as the ST sees fit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T04:57:07-07:00","id":570163,"title":"","content":"I suppose that is true enough. However, in my experience the newest breed of tabletop gamer (Post 3.0 D&amp;D and younger) is woefully narrow minded in their game scholarship. It's a different subject but there seems to be this propensity to either adhere blindly to exactly what is in book or be completely blind to things that are not expressly written down. For instance 2nd Edition Forsaken states that the Forsaken chose the name and call themselves Forsaken of their own volition. That's patently wrong. No one calls <i>themselves</i> Forsaken of their own free will. Their enemies <i>proclaim</i> them to be Forsaken. It is only centuries later with the Forsaken claiming the term from their enemies and making it their own that they would self identify as Forsaken, as if to say &quot;I am Forsaken, but unlike you I can be redeemed.&quot; But there are those who, seeing the text say one thing will just blindly assume that is true. If Beast specifically says the Beasts are both from the dark mother and know the truth of the nWoD some people will assume that is true rather than being an assumption by the Beasts as a response to try and understand their existence. I'm not looking forward to being the one who has to remind people constantly that the nWoD is not a monolith but a continuum of in-character beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:13:23-07:00","id":570166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/570139-beast-question?p=570154#post570154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages assume that everything is somehow connected to the Supernal, and originates from, or reflects it, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, quite the opposite. You're mistaking a tiny number of mage's fans for the game. <br /> <br /> Beasts, now, Beasts are clearly just as to the Astral what Sin-Eaters and Werewolves are to the Underworld and Shadow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:20:17-07:00","id":570167,"title":"","content":"I think they toned it down in the revised edition of Beast. Beasts seem more like cousin than big brother. All the games do seem to get a bit elitist when it comes to other supes so it wasn't unexpected, but it didn't really fit with the whole concept of Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:31:31-07:00","id":570170,"title":"","content":"That's much more preferable. The reason it sticks with me specifically in relation to Forsaken as my go-to venue is that at the start of the nWoD cycle Forsaken suffered from a lot of lingering Apocalypse hate and Apocalypse cronyism about werewolves being the ultimate antisocial murder machines when in fact the Forsaken specifically are among the most likely supernatural to accept another supernatural. Its the Pure, with their inflated numbers and their zealous society that have painted werewolves in a corner because you're almost four times as likely as a non-werewolf to encounter the Pure if at all. If you do encounter the Fosaken, they're usually so busy trying to spin all those spirit and reality plates simultaneously they don't have time to fight with other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> But if a would-be supernatural ally colors their presence with elitism (looking at you, Kindred), the werewolves are just as likely to react very poorly.<br /> <br /> &quot;Does it damage the spirit world?&quot;<br /> &quot;No.&quot;<br /> &quot;Does it damage the territory?&quot;<br /> &quot;It does eat things.&quot;<br /> &quot;But does it kill more than it can eat?&quot;<br /> &quot;No.&quot;<br /> &quot;Is it actively making my job harder?&quot;<br /> &quot;No.&quot;<br /> &quot;And you say it wants to help us out?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> &quot;Well damn bud, pull up a chair, lets get this critter a beer.&quot;<br /> &quot;Why thank you little brother.&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;... What did you call me?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Beast and Forsaken can benefit a lot from one another, and I want to see them both do really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:40:19-07:00","id":570181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RuneKnight3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/570139-beast-question?p=570163#post570163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that is true enough. However, in my experience the newest breed of tabletop gamer (Post 3.0 D&amp;D and younger) is woefully narrow minded in their game scholarship. (...) But there are those who, seeing the text say one thing will just blindly assume that is true. If Beast specifically says the Beasts are both from the dark mother and know the truth of the nWoD some people will assume that is true rather than being an assumption by the Beasts as a response to try and understand their existence. I'm not looking forward to being the one who has to remind people constantly that the nWoD is not a monolith but a continuum of in-character beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe those people should learn reading comprehension and critical thinking then. If they're narrowminded then that's where the problem lies, not in the writing. And the books should absolutely not conform to the lowest common denominator. The World of Darkness is a grim and ambiguous place, full of questionable thoughts, where nothing fits in neat little boxes.<br /> <br /> The kickstarter also has a lot of &quot;Beasts believe&quot; and &quot;Beasts think&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-27-2015, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:47:19-07:00","id":570183,"title":"","content":"I agree. I mean really. I could tell tale of some of the stupid that has come out of the mouths of perfectly rational people who could only see through narrow boxes. The thing is that in my observations part of the reason for the pervasiveness of the problem is writers unintentionally taking for granted that their readership is neccessarily as schooled as it should be in its own subject matter. Using D&amp;D again as the meta example, 3.0 and to a lesser extent 4.0 (An entirely different series of major mistakes there) didn't expressly prohibit some older more nuanced material from 2nd and 1st Edition D&amp;D. There were game concepts hard learned and spread by word of mouth through the player base that everyone knew were part and parcel of the older editions that just didn't make it into the newer ones, and so newer players assumed they were nonexistent or had never been there. Its the same mentality that looked at cWoD and nWoD and said &quot;Well they're both WoD, they must be the same&quot;, when we know they are very much not. I would just not want to see Beast suffer from misunderstandings due to a lack of clarity that seems to imply things which it really does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:48:14-07:00","id":570184,"title":"","content":"I'm talking about the stereotypes that they always do. The first version had Beasts looking down on most and now there seems to be a decent level of respect. They haven't revised the chapters dealing with crossover, but I recall them saying they were going to give it another look. I'm definitely getting more of a Nightbreed and Adam's Family vibe than before. I can't say how close they will get in the end until they finish. All indications suggest that the developers are aware of the concern on that point. They've done a good job of addressing most of the other points. The rest haven't really come up yet as they are mainly in the back of the book.<br /> <br /> Werewolves and Beasts would seem like natural pals in some respects, but they also have a point of conflict. Beasts likely create some of the darker spirits with their feeding. If a pack doesn't approve then they have problems. Then again, some werewolves would be happy to have the help feeding those types of spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-27-2015, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:52:37-07:00","id":570185,"title":"","content":"That really makes me jazzy. Nightbreed is, sadly, a terrible movie when compared to the source material in the novel CABAL, but it had great notions that could have likewise gone great places. I really like the idea of monsters that are straight up <i>monsters</i> but would rather live quietly out of the way rather than actively compete with humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:06:21-07:00","id":570188,"title":"","content":"I liked the concepts behind Nightbreed. It wasn't very well executed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:56:08-07:00","id":570239,"title":"","content":"I didn't think the original preview suffered from any clarity issues myself, but the revisions definitely seem to clarify some points (and clean up the subtext so that the intended reading is more transparent).<br /> <br /> Just... I don't get how some people could think that Beast tries to enforce a uniform cosmology anymore than the other lines. It doesn't touch or attempt to explain the greater cosmology of most of the splats, even less so subdue any of it. What it does is concile the existence of all the other monsters as related to Beasts (or not, as is the case of the Unchained), from their own unique perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:05:48-07:00","id":571186,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cThe children now love luxury. They have bad manners, contempt for authority; they show disrespect for elders and love chatter in place of exercise.\u201d</span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Runeknight3</span><br /> <br /> (I know this quote is almost certainly misattributed to socrates but I still think of it whenever I read stuff like &quot;I suppose that is true enough. However, in my experience the newest breed of tabletop gamer (Post 3.0 D&amp;D and younger) is woefully narrow minded in their game scholarship.&quot; )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3497-urbicamortis","name":"UrbicaMortis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:05:58-07:00","id":572610,"title":"","content":"Overall, the tone of Beast is way less condescending than I'd feared it would be when I first saw the crossover fuel bits of it. The impression I have is that they see most of the other supernaturals as a <i>younger</i> sibling or cousin, not a 'little brother/sister' in the sense of an irritating rugrat. They're a more specialized form of creature, where the Beasts are (they think) older and less defined. It isn't a matter of looking down on them and more one of working out how the family tree fits together.<br /> <br /> If they were to get into the subject at all with a bunch of Uratha they just met, it'd probably be along the lines of 'So, we think we're descended from the same Mother who bore Father Wolf, which kinda makes us cousins from our perspective. Some of our powers seem to support the idea there's a shared history of <i>some</i> sort anyway, I dunno. I just found out about all this last month and I wanted to give you guys a hand clearing out the spider monsters that are wearing my neighbors like cheap suit. You in?'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}